# .config/mise/lib/forbidden-names.txt.example
# COMMITTED template for the gitignored .config/mise/lib/forbidden-names.txt.
#
# Copy this to forbidden-names.txt and add any truly-private literals locally:
#   cp .config/mise/lib/forbidden-names.txt.example .config/mise/lib/forbidden-names.txt
#
# The private-names guard (the validate:private-names task) reads the working
# copy (forbidden-names.txt), ORs every non-comment line into a single regex, and
# fails the build on any match in the tracked tree. Both the guard script and the
# working list self-exclude from the scan.
#
# This template documents the CATEGORIES of forbidden tokens without leaking any
# specific private value. The generic regexes below are publication-safe defaults;
# keep org/customer/device-specific literals OUT of this committed template and add
# them only to your local (gitignored) forbidden-names.txt.
#
# Format: one POSIX-ERE / rg regex per non-comment, non-blank line.

# === Category: private org / handle / customer names ===
# Add your own org name, GitHub handle local-part, and customer prefixes locally,
# e.g. a literal like `acme-internal` or a customer prefix `customer-[a-z0-9]`.
# (No example literal is shipped here on purpose.)

# === Category: network identity (tailnet / overlay hostnames) ===
\.ts\.net
# Add literal tailnet hostnames locally if you want belt-and-suspenders coverage.

# === Category: alternate VM runtime forbidden by spec (lab is Lima) ===
# (?i:...) keeps the match case-insensitive so capitalized prose variants are caught.
\b(?i:colima)\b

# === Category: frozen / paywalled Bitnami artifacts ===
bitnamilegacy
bitnami/kubectl

# === Category: NodePort service surface (the lab is port-forward only) ===
# Match the manifest FORM, not the bare word, so prohibition prose in docs
# ("no NodePort") does not false-positive.
type:[[:space:]]*NodePort
nodePort:

# === Category: forbidden environment label (must be ai-infra-platform-local) ===
# Match the leak FORM (key=value), not the bare token.
deployment\.environment=local-dev

# === Category: real absolute home paths ===
# Add a literal real home-path prefix locally if a non-placeholder one slips in,
# e.g. `/Users/<your-name>`. The placeholders <repo-root>, $HOME, and mac-local
# are the only allowed substitutes (IMPL-BRIEF §4).
